{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["הפדיום — the mem is superfluous, like the mem of ריקם. הכנם. שלשום. They were the three hundred by which the Levites exceeded twenty-two thousand firstborns. And no firstborn disqualifies [another] firstborn — thus our Rabbis interpret it."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The lemmas הכנם and שלשום appear to be cited Hebrew forms; they are rendered here in Hebrew script as they stand without translation, following the instruction to preserve Hebrew forms. The phrase 'ואין בכור מפקיע בכור' is rendered literally; the meaning is that a firstborn of a Levite mother does not remove firstborn status from another."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:45.151014559Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}